== ui_card "Quick Start Guide"
  p Welcome to Slim-Pickins! This guide will get you up and running with the framework in less than 5 minutes.

  h3 1. Installation
  p Add the gem to your <code>Gemfile</code>:

  == ui_code 'gem "slim-pickins"'

  p And run:
  == ui_code "bundle install"

  h3 2. Asset Setup
  p Slim-Pickins relies on <strong>Stimulus</strong> for interactivity and <strong>SortableJS</strong> for drag-and-drop lists. You supply both; the library imports them as bare specifiers.

  p Map them in your import map:
  == ui_code do
    | {
        "imports": {
          "@hotwired/stimulus": "/js/vendor/stimulus.js",
          "sortablejs": "/js/vendor/sortable.esm.js"
        }
      }

  p Then register the library's controllers on your Stimulus application:
  == ui_code do
    | // application.js
      import { Application } from "@hotwired/stimulus"
      import { registerSlimPickins } from "/assets/js/slim_pickins.js"

      const application = Application.start()
      registerSlimPickins(application)

  h3 3. Configuration
  p In your main application file (e.g., <code>app.rb</code> for Sinatra), register the extension:

  == ui_code do
    | class App < Sinatra::Base
        register SlimPickins
        # ...
      end

  p This also mounts the asset middleware, which serves the stylesheet and the controllers above from the gem at <code>/assets</code>.

  h3 4. Your First Component
  p Now you can use the helpers in your Slim templates!

  .sp-card.sp-card--accent
    .sp-card__body
      h4 Example: User Profile Card
      p Copy and paste this into any view:

      == ui_code do
        | == ui_card "User Profile" do
            .sp-cluster
              span Name: Jane Doe
              == ui_button "Edit", :neutral

  h3 Next Steps
  p Ready to build? Explore the core components:

  .sp-cluster
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/button" Buttons
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/card" Cards
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/form" Forms
